			<div class="wp-block-comment-date"><time datetime="2026-07-06T18:52:58-04:00"><a href="https://www.theflavorbender.com/easy-homemade-chicken-ramen/comment-page-9/#comment-194612">July 6, 2026</a></time></div>

			
		</div>
		

		<div class="wp-block-comment-content"><p>I had a doctor&#8217;s appointment across the street from a big Asian market this morning. While in the waiting room, I Goggled &#8220;Homemade Chicken Ramen Recipe&#8221; and yours popped up. In the market, I bought chicken thighs, dark soy sauce, rice cooking wine, chili garlic sauce, fresh and dried shitakes, Asian baby bok choy, fresh Kyoto ramen noodles, bean sprouts and radishes. I also got a big package of chicken feet and made homemade broth in the electric pressure cooker. Between the chicken broth, the glazed chicken, chopping the veggies, making the Shayu broth, the soy eggs which I let marinate 2 hours, and boiling the noodles, it took almost 4 hours. But it was so worth it. I and my family loved it. My wife called dibs on the leftovers to bring to work tomorrow.</p>
</div>

		<div class="wp-block-comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-194612" data-commentid="194612" data-postid="25902" data-belowelement="comment-194612" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Jim Kelleher" aria-label="Reply to Jim Kelleher">Reply</a></div>
	</div>
	
	</li><li id="comment-192094" class="comment odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1">
	
	<div class="wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-e02479de wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained" style="margin-top: var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)">
		<div class="wp-block-comment-author-name">Matt</div>

		
		<div class="wp-block-group has-custom-contrast-light-color has-text-color has-link-color has-x-small-font-size wp-elements-12 is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-8032b07a wp-block-group-is-layout-flex" style="font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: uppercase">
			<div class="wp-block-comment-date"><time datetime="2026-05-20T16:32:46-04:00"><a href="https://www.theflavorbender.com/easy-homemade-chicken-ramen/comment-page-9/#comment-192094">May 20, 2026</a></time></div>

			
		</div>
		

		<div class="wp-block-comment-content"><p>Ummmmm everything is excellent and amazing ramen! EXCEPT!!!! Do NOT put 1 TBS pepper flakes…..I legit put sriracha and hot sauce on everything I eat but I did half that amount and it was still crazy spicy!!! I cannot imagine doing a full tablespoon of red pepper flakes that is wild! You will burn your lips off!! Clearly they never tested the recipe with chili flakes.</p>
</div>

		<div class="wp-block-comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-192094" data-commentid="192094" data-postid="25902" data-belowelement="comment-192094" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Matt" aria-label="Reply to Matt">Reply</a></div>
	</div>
	
	<ol><li id="comment-192113" class="comment byuser comment-author-dini bypostauthor even depth-2">
	
	<div class="wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-e02479de wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained" style="margin-top: var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)">
		<div class="wp-block-comment-author-name"><a rel="external nofollow ugc" href="https://www.theflavorbender.com" target="_self" >Dini Kodippili</a></div>

		
		<div class="wp-block-group has-custom-contrast-light-color has-text-color has-link-color has-x-small-font-size wp-elements-13 is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-8032b07a wp-block-group-is-layout-flex" style="font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: uppercase">
			<div class="wp-block-comment-date"><time datetime="2026-05-20T20:23:22-04:00"><a href="https://www.theflavorbender.com/easy-homemade-chicken-ramen/comment-page-9/#comment-192113">May 20, 2026</a></time></div>

			
		</div>
		

		<div class="wp-block-comment-content"><p>Hi Matt<br />
I&#8217;m so glad you enjoyed the recipe! But we DO enjoy this with lots of chili in it, because we love spicy food, and 1 tbsp pf chili flakes isn&#8217;t too spicy for us at all. Sriracha isn&#8217;t spicy for us at all, so maybe we do like our foods spicier than most.<br />
Which is why I did state to omit or adjust it to your liking 🙂<br />
However, there is going to be some variability in the spice levels depending on the type of chili flakes you use as well. Some brands have mostly seeds, instead of a mix of seeds and the chili skin. More seeds in your chili flakes will make it spicier. So it really depends on the brand.<br />
I hope that helps for next time!</p>
</div>

		<div class="wp-block-comment-reply-link"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-192113" data-commentid="192113" data-postid="25902" data-belowelement="comment-192113" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Dini Kodippili" aria-label="Reply to Dini Kodippili">Reply</a></div>
	</div>
	
	</li></ol></li><li id="comment-190249" class="comment odd alt thread-even depth-1">
	
	<div class="wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-e02479de wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained" style="margin-top: var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)">
		<div class="wp-block-comment-author-name">Sharon</div>

		
