			<div class="wp-block-comment-date"><time datetime="2026-02-08T22:54:01-05:00"><a href="https://www.theflavorbender.com/easy-homemade-chicken-ramen/comment-page-9/#comment-184772">February 8, 2026</a></time></div>

			
		</div>
		

		<div class="wp-block-comment-content"><p><img decoding="async" class="wprm-comment-rating perfmatters-lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='80'%20height='16'%20viewBox='0%200%2080%2016'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="5 stars" width="80" height="16" data-src="https://www.theflavorbender.com/wp-content/plugins/wp-recipe-maker/assets/icons/rating/stars-alt-5.svg" /><br />
Fabulous! I’ve made a lot of Ramen from scratch and always in the search of a ramen recipe that’s easy, delicious, and customizable. This one hits the mark. The broth with homemade chicken stock is outstanding, I don’t think slicing and returning the dried shiitake to the broth adds a lot because I also had fresh mushrooms. The soy glazed chicken is to die for, I’m saving extras for fried rice as suggested. Thank you!</p>
